<?xml version="1.0"?>
<labwc_config>

  <!-- labwc-autostart rotates the DSI panel's *display* output 90deg CCW
       (wlr-randr's transform flag, output DSI-1, value 90), but that
       doesn't rotate the touch digitizer's coordinates to match - taps
       land in the wrong place relative to what's visually shown, even
       though gesture-relative interactions like pinch-zoom still "work"
       since they only read relative motion between two touch points, not
       absolute position.

       IMPORTANT: every rotation value tried before this one silently had
       zero effect - the file had a syntax error (a literal double-hyphen
       inside this very comment, which XML forbids in comment content, not
       just the "wlr-randr" example above's flags) that made labwc reject
       the whole file and fall back to defaults every single boot,
       regardless of what the calibrationMatrix said. Confirmed via
       labwc's own debug log: "read config file ... rc.xml" immediately
       followed by "error parsing config file". If touch ever needs
       recalibrating again, verify the file actually parses (that log
       line) before assuming the matrix value itself is wrong.

       Tried so far, testing each on the real hardware (none confirmed
       correct yet, since none of them were actually being applied):
       90deg CW, 180deg, a computed 45deg CCW matrix, removing calibration
       entirely, and now 90deg CCW - this is the first one being tested
       with the parse error actually fixed, so treat all prior "results"
       as meaningless. -->
  <libinput>
    <device category="touch">
      <calibrationMatrix>0 1 0 -1 0 1</calibrationMatrix>
    </device>
  </libinput>

</labwc_config>
